      "id": 1,
      "claim": "The minimum cross-sectional diameter of an intact adult human skull is approximately 11-12 cm.",
      "evidence": "Anthropometric data indicates that while the biparietal diameter is ~14-15 cm, the narrowest dimension (often near the foramen magnum or occipital region) is still typically 11-12 cm. Even in cases of extreme microcephaly, the rigid bony structure rarely falls below the pelvic inlet dimensions.",
      "weight": 0.4,
